-# BOOTHFORGE AI
+# BOOTHFORGE AI — private pilot
 
-**Phase 1 development scaffold** — responsive Arabic project dashboard + FastAPI project API.
+The repaired pilot is in `apps/web` (Next.js) and `services/api` (FastAPI).
+The Vite prototype in `src`, its package files, the root prototype and the original ZIP are preserved.
+All repairs live on `boothforge-development`; do not merge into `main` until reviewed.
 
-## Run locally
+## What works
 
-Requires Python 3.11+ and Node.js 20+.
+- Arabic, RTL project dashboard with booth dimensions, validated area, reception counters, screens, meeting rooms, storage and notes.
+- Browser requests go to same-origin `/api`; the backend address and internal bearer token stay on the server.
+- Password-protected pilot: the custom Node server protects pages, static assets and APIs. The API route checks authentication independently, validates POST origins, limits request size and does not forward browser credentials upstream.
+- FastAPI separately verifies an internal bearer token. Its deployment listener is loopback only.
+- SQLite transactions preserve concurrent writes and survive process restarts when the data directory is retained.
+- Raster brand uploads accept real PNG/JPEG pixels, enforce 5 MB / 16 megapixel limits, strip metadata and appended content, and remain outside public web directories. SVG/PDF are intentionally blocked until a safe processing pipeline exists.
+- AI requests explicitly return 501. No generated images, CAD outputs or paid provider calls are simulated or enabled.
+
+This is a **single trusted team** pilot with a shared login, not a multi-customer platform. Use synthetic data only on the supplied free hosting configuration.
+
+## One-click Windows startup / blank-page troubleshooting
+
+Extract the entire delivery ZIP into a new folder. Double-click `START_BOOTHFORGE_WINDOWS.cmd` from the repository root. The launcher verifies Python 3.11+ and Node.js 22+, prepares the local Python environment and web dependencies, starts both loopback-only services and opens the correct dashboard URL automatically. Keep its console open; Ctrl+C stops the services.
+
+Do not open `index.html` as a standalone application. The preserved root prototype references `/src/main.tsx`, while the usable dashboard is a Next.js application in `boothforge-ai/apps/web`. Source TSX requires the framework development/build server. `OPEN_BOOTHFORGE.html` is an offline startup guide, not a static export of the app.
+
+The launcher changes no existing `.env` file and makes no AI requests. Initial setup needs internet access for Python/npm packages. It selects nearby free local ports if the defaults are occupied. It does not configure hosting or a public listener. The Python launcher startup was verified locally; the Windows `.cmd` wrapper still requires confirmation on the user's Windows device.
+
+To verify an existing installation without opening a browser, run `python scripts/start_local.py --skip-install --smoke` from this `boothforge-ai` directory. This uses disposable data and stops both servers after the check.
+
+## Local development
+
+Requires Node.js 22+ and Python 3.11+. Run commands from this `boothforge-ai` directory.
+
+Terminal 1, macOS/Linux:
 
