+```
+
+Terminal 2:
+
 ```bash
 cd apps/web
-npm install
-npm run dev
+npm ci
+```
+
+Set `BOOTHFORGE_ENV=development` (`$env:BOOTHFORGE_ENV='development'` in PowerShell), then run `npm run dev`.
+Open **http://localhost:3000**. Both listeners default to loopback. This explicit local mode bypasses login; never expose it to the internet.
+Use the same hostname/port in `APP_ORIGIN` if changing the URL. `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` is no longer used.
+API documentation and OpenAPI routes are disabled in this pilot.
+
+## Verification
+
+From `services/api`:
+
+```bash
+.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q
+```
+
+From `apps/web`:
+
+```bash
+npm ci
+npm run typecheck
+npm test
+npm run build
+npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high
+```
+
+After building, from `services/api` (ports 8000 and 3100 must be free):
+
+```bash
+.venv/bin/python ../../scripts/smoke_test.py
 ```
 
-Open http://localhost:3000 and API documentation at http://localhost:8000/docs.
+On Windows use `.\.venv\Scripts\python` instead of `.venv/bin/python`.
+The smoke test launches both production-mode services, uses disposable generated credentials and synthetic data, exercises authentication/CSRF/project persistence paths, verifies AI remains disabled and stops the services afterwards. It never prints credentials.
+
+## Desktop and mobile browser tests
+
+Install Chromium with `npx playwright install chromium` from `apps/web` (add `--with-deps` on a Linux runner when needed). Build the frontend first. The harness requires OpenSSL and free local ports 8000, 3100 and 3443.
+
+From `services/api`, run:
+
+```bash
+.venv/bin/python ../../scripts/browser_test.py
+```
+
+The harness generates disposable local TLS credentials, starts the real production-mode services, tests both viewport sizes and cleans up its synthetic data. `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` optionally selects an already-installed Chromium binary; `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_ARGS` optionally supplies a JSON array of runner-specific launch arguments. Do not pass real provider keys. Screenshots and test output stay in ignored `test-results/` and are not included in project deliverables.
+
+## Private online deployment preparation
+
+See [deploy/PRIVATE_PREVIEW.md](deploy/PRIVATE_PREVIEW.md). The prepared Docker-based Render configuration is **not deployed** and automatic deploys are disabled.
+Provider API keys are not required for this milestone. Do not put them in source, browser fields, `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, images, ZIPs or chat messages. The launcher removes OpenAI/Google/Gemini provider variables from the pilot child processes while AI generation is disabled.
 
