+# Private preview deployment — prepared, not applied
+
+## Proposed workload
+
+One Docker web service runs Next.js and FastAPI under a supervisor. Only the Next.js listener is exposed; FastAPI binds `127.0.0.1:8000`. The supervisor stops both services if either exits. Render must terminate TLS in front of the Node listener.
+
+`render.preview.yaml` targets branch `boothforge-development`, uses `plan: free`, disables automatic deploys and exposes only a minimal anonymous `/health` probe. All other URLs, including static assets, require HTTP Basic login.
+
+This creates an internet-reachable address with authenticated access. It is an application-private pilot, not a private-network service. The sample has **no persistent disk**: data can disappear on restart/redeploy/idle suspension. Use fabricated client names and disposable brand images only.
+
+No service, deployment, subscription, domain or paid API request has been created by this change.
+
+## Activation checklist for the operator
+
+1. Keep the repaired branch separate; do not merge or overwrite the legacy project. Read the test report first.
+2. Build the Docker image in a Docker-capable runner before activation. The development environment used for these repairs did not include Docker.
+3. In Render, select the repaired branch and Blueprint path `boothforge-ai/deploy/render.preview.yaml` explicitly. The original default-branch project has no deployment file; do not use an unqualified one-click link.
+4. Review the current account plan, free-service limits and any build/bandwidth charges. Obtain user approval before any paid resource or public unauthenticated release. The supplied file explicitly selects the free compute plan; it must not be silently upgraded.
+5. Fill secrets in Render's secure Environment settings, never GitHub or chat:
+
+| Variable | Required value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `PREVIEW_USERNAME` | A dedicated pilot username |
+| `PREVIEW_PASSWORD` | A unique random password, at least 24 characters |
+| `API_TOKEN` | Generated by Render (`generateValue: true`), at least 32 characters |
+| `APP_ORIGIN` | Exact final HTTPS origin, e.g. `https://your-pilot.onrender.com`, without trailing slash |
+| `BOOTHFORGE_ENV` | `preview` |
+
+6. Do not set `BOOTHFORGE_ENV=development` on hosting. Do not run `next start` or `next dev` directly as the public entry point: use the Docker CMD / `scripts/run_preview.py` / `npm start` custom server.
+7. Activate only the protected test-data pilot. Before sharing the URL, verify: anonymous root/API/static requests return 401, a wrong password fails, authorized creation works, a foreign/missing POST Origin returns 403, AI returns 501 and no credentials appear in page HTML/network responses.
+8. Share pilot access only with the owner/approved team. HTTP Basic has no per-user roles, audit trail or reliable logout; close the browser session or rotate the credentials when ending access.
+9. Remove disposable data by replacing the test container/data directory; keep provider adapters disabled until cost approval and server-only credential configuration are complete.
+
+## Before real customer data
+
+This pilot deliberately does not claim production readiness. Add individual accounts and tenant isolation, an approved hosting region, encryption/retention/deletion policy, persistent storage and tested backups, audit logs, edge rate limits, malware processing where required, and a reviewed data migration. Obtain approval for the associated hosting/storage/API costs first.
+
+The local login rate limiter uses the connection IP and does not trust spoofable forwarding headers. Behind a shared reverse proxy, its 20 failed attempts/minute can throttle the whole pilot. A proper edge identity/rate-limit service is required before broader use.
+
+## Validation boundaries
+
+- The Blueprint was validated against the current public Render JSON schema.
+- Render CLI/account-aware validation and an actual Docker image build were not run in this environment; the CLI and Docker daemon were absent.
+- Desktop/mobile browser tests ran over disposable localhost HTTPS with a headless Chromium binary; screenshots contain synthetic data only and are excluded from deliverables.
+- Applying a Blueprint is a deployment action; schema validation alone does not create anything.
+- A persistent disk is intentionally omitted. No real customer-data durability or multi-tenant security claim is made.
+
+Official references: [Blueprints](https://render.com/docs/blueprint-spec), [secrets](https://render.com/docs/configure-environment-variables), [free services](https://render.com/docs/free), [Next.js self-hosting](https://nextjs.org/docs/15/app/guides/self-hosting).
