+
+Baseline: `ccb58e810c09ba2cddc4ad771b3e96417a860a3f` on `main`.
+Repairs: isolated **local** branch `boothforge-development`. GitHub rejected remote branch creation with HTTP 403 (`Resource not accessible by integration`), so no remote branch or pull request was created.
+
+| Check | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| FastAPI regression/security tests | 17 passed |
+| Node authentication/origin tests | 4 passed |
+| Chromium browser tests over local HTTPS | 8 passed across desktop and mobile viewports: project creation/requirements, dimension limits, escaped markup, connection-error recovery |
+| Visual inspection of desktop/mobile renders | Passed; fixed small-screen touch controls and reviewed responsive layout |
+| One-click local startup launcher | Passed on the local Linux runtime: started Next.js and FastAPI, rendered the dashboard and verified the API proxy with disposable data. Windows CMD wrapper not executed on Windows. |
+| TypeScript type check | Passed |
+| Next.js production build | Passed, Next.js 15.5.28 / React 19.3.1 |
+| Real Next.js + FastAPI HTTP smoke test | 38 checks passed, including unauthorized access, same-origin creation, CSRF rejection, disabled generation, internal bearer auth and failed-login throttling |
+| npm production dependency audit | 0 known vulnerabilities after overriding PostCSS to 8.5.32 |
+| Python production dependency audit (`pip-audit -r requirements.txt`) | No known vulnerabilities found |
+| Render Blueprint current JSON-schema validation | Passed |
+| Original ZIP hash comparison | Identical SHA-256: `c8305532817ba7ef8d22dd160340108881f15f86ef5c925f91bbf851c0896cb8` |
+| Original root/Vite sources | Unchanged |
+| Live provider/API spending | None; provider adapters remain disabled |
+| Internet deployment | Not applied |
+
+Limitations: the API test suite emits a Starlette deprecation warning for its httpx-based test client. The initial Chromium CDN download failed; browser testing was subsequently completed with a local Chromium 153 test binary. Docker image build and Render account-aware/CLI validation could not run because those tools were absent. HTTP smoke tests exercised the actual production processes locally; they are not a substitute for these remaining deployment checks.
+
+All test projects/images were fabricated. No real customer data or provider key was used. Main is not merged or modified.
+
+Windows startup follow-up: the owner confirmed successful startup after replacing `uvicorn[standard]` with minimal `uvicorn`. Optional Uvicorn extras pulled in a PyYAML source build under Python 3.15, requesting Visual C++ unnecessarily for this app. The runtime requirements now contain this same fix.
